OL,3,GNEWSAThe slow, muddy work of saving
OL,4,Aancient bogs
OL,5,
OL,6,FHigh up on a Manx hillside, Sarah
OL,7,FHickey effortlessly pushes a metre-long
OL,8,Fmetal rod into the wet ground until it
OL,9,Fdisappears almost to her hands.
OL,11,F"This is pretty deep here," she says,
OL,12,Freading the markings on the probe.
OL,13,FBeneath her boots is peat, built up
OL,14,Fover thousands of years and consisting
OL,15,Fof partially decayed plants and organic
OL,16,Fmatter.
OL,18,FHickey is the island's Peatland Officer
OL,19,Fand part of an Uplands team of just
OL,20,Fthree, who, between them, manage about
OL,21,F8,000 hectares of the Island's hills.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB IOM NewsC Reg TVF Clean Feed
